# Rust/SBF build artifacts
programs/counter/target/

# Compiled program output. counter.so IS committed on purpose: the CI image has
# no Rust toolchain, and cargo-build-sbf lives inside @effectstream/solana-node's
# vendor/ dir, which is only populated when the validator binary downloads — i.e.
# after this build step runs. Same convention as
# e2e/shared/contracts/near/test_event_contract.wasm and
# e2e/shared/contracts/solana/test_event.so. Rebuild with `bun run build:solana`
# after editing programs/counter/src/lib.rs.
/build/*
!/build/counter.so

# solana-test-validator scratch ledger
test-ledger/

# rustfmt backups
**/*.rs.bk

# Keypairs. `keypair/counter-program.json` IS committed on purpose so the
# program ID stays deterministic for local dev — its secret is public and it
# must never own anything on a real network. Any OTHER keypair stays out.
keypair/*.json
!keypair/counter-program.json
